  "catalog_course_description": "Quantum effects in low dimensional systems and nanostructures, pseudo-two dimensional systems and superlattices, quantum wires, quantum dots, quantum transport theory, Kubo equation, localization, universal conductance fluctuations, Aharonov-Bohm effect, single electron phenomena, quantum Hall effects, Kondo effect.",
  "course_learning_outcomes": [
    "Upon completion of this course, students will be able to: (i) explain and discuss basic phenomena in the mesoscale physics (ii) calculate conductance of simple nanoscale conductors (iii) follow research papers in the field"
